.TH ZENITH 8 "October 2026" "Zenith 1.2.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
zenith \- Ultra-low latency Linux gaming optimizer daemon (C++20)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zenith
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zenith
is a high-performance, non-intrusive Linux background daemon designed to minimize frame-time jitter, micro-stutters, and input latency for native and Proton/Wine gaming workloads.
.PP
Zenith listens for process lifecycle events via Netlink proc connector, detects running games, and dynamically optimizes CPU core topology (AMD 3D V-Cache CCD pinning, Intel P-core prioritization), memory management, GPU clock power states, IRQ affinities, and PipeWire audio buffers.
.PP
Zenith uses a crash-only architecture with a Write-Ahead Log (WAL) located at
\fI/run/zenith/journal.json\fR, ensuring that all kernel mutations are atomically and safely reverted when games exit or if the daemon unexpectedly terminates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Specify custom configuration path (default: \fI/etc/zenith/zenith.conf\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " \fINAME\fR"
Force active optimization profile (\fBsafe\fR, \fBbalanced\fR, or \fBaggressive\fR).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground rather than as a background service.
.TP
.BR \-\-rollback
Execute emergency rollback of all recorded mutations recorded in the WAL journal and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Simulate optimization decisions and log target actions without writing to sysfs or procfs.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/zenith/zenith.conf
Global daemon configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/zenith/profiles.conf
Profile definitions and parameter overrides.
.TP
.I /run/zenith/zenith.sock
UNIX domain socket for IPC communication with \fBzenithctl\fR.
.TP
.I /run/zenith/journal.json
Atomic state journal (Write-Ahead Log) for crash recovery.
.TP
.I /run/zenith/zenith.lock
POSIX advisory lock file ensuring single-instance execution.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
Gracefully terminates the daemon, triggering an immediate and atomic rollback of all applied kernel and hardware tweaks.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reloads configuration files and re-evaluates active gaming sessions.
